{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/verification.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:34:34.165824Z","id":"7081ac09c683ef93c85d3b251d305fb9141ee4180cbe604b224348fe9b1ef900","body":{"detail":"§10.1 drives a real `claude -p` with this branch's plugin against a scratch daemon and a scripted Messages API that calls the publish tool, then replies as a LAN viewer with curl and validates the export with Ajv. Unlike scripts/smoke-claude-ask.sh, its fake model (a variant of scripts/fake-anthropic.py whose first turn calls `mcp__plugin_clax_clax__publish`) and its driver were not committed, so the check is described, not rerunnable as is. A scripts/smoke-claude-toolpath.sh, reusing fake-anthropic.py with a publish scenario, would make it repeatable.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1085},"end":{"line":1100},"content_hash":"2a2bc6f18be95108c6873fc23dd7f10d97f1cebac973297f961d3f8979d1de8b"},"summary":"The Toolpath manual check (§10.1) has no script in the repository","tags":["verification","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:11.811733Z","id":"06d36deac10389c296e42470276d7a5f535689b98d1be753d0be1f645f583d9d","body":{"detail":"Added for the shell: participants agents' name and person ({public_id, name, owner}); a thread owner's person_name; a thread's approves_first (public IDs, null for the owner; browsers only, absent when empty); and owner: true on GET /api/viewers/me and the artifact boot payload's viewer for the owner's browser. Agents' payloads change only by the name and person keys spec 2026-10-08 section 19 item 6 allows.","kind":"concern","summary":"The contract does not yet describe the fields the Send menu and owner chip read","tags":["task:24","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:42.668690Z","id":"35572e2274d3fc3b78b5fe674c391f6b9d2183a26a7f9d6a0c39d06971a1e776","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"06d36deac10389c296e42470276d7a5f535689b98d1be753d0be1f645f583d9d","summary":"Since bb547990: thread views no longer carry approves_first; the new browser-only route GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/approves-first?threads=<tid,…> answers {approves_first: [public ID | null]} (403 for LAN viewers, anonymous callers and agents; 404 for a thread of another artifact; at most 200 threads). Question views and inbox items' agent gain name; browsers get people's names as stored, agents the payload-safe form.","tags":["task:24","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:04.319721Z","id":"d74a29be48f8826b30999dbe3bf8a9e7486f491197c67db70c9b595700e55335","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs (the status tool's annotations) changed status to read_only_hint false, destructive false, idempotent true, because `name` writes. Under Codex's `writes` approval mode (crates/clax-cli/src/codex_approvals.rs:12) a tool not annotated readOnlyHint asks, so status, which ran unasked, now prompts; docs/contract.md:56 still says readOnlyHint true.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":61},"content_hash":"966a28b85777889409a04e068b00adbd01e067425963e6aedf0515c1a43859cb"},"suggested_fix":"Move status to the destructiveHint false list in docs/contract.md and say there that `writes` mode asks for it.","summary":"The contract still lists status among the readOnlyHint tools, but status is now annotated read_only_hint = false","tags":["review","docs","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:55:01.457198Z","id":"e104b84998514f5d815bba578eba18ce20226e26f2a33019af423d45e7df973d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7a06e2cd","summary":"The contract now lists status as not read-only (destructiveHint false, idempotentHint true) because it names the agent with `name`, and comments_handoff among the state-changing tools (7a06e2cd).","supersedes":"d74a29be48f8826b30999dbe3bf8a9e7486f491197c67db70c9b595700e55335","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:07:31.464183Z","id":"b49fdc77c91f68d06fd9447da725617e40cffcd4fe5b5b544b833edd4aa66d67","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:28338345","summary":"docs/contract.md now describes them (28338345): participants' agents carry name and person {public_id, name, owner} ('Versions, seen marks and attention'); a thread's owner {handle, name, person, live, person_name} ('Thread ownership'); GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/approves-first?threads= and who learns it ('Approvals'); owner: true on GET /api/viewers/me and the boot payload's viewer ('Security model'); the question view's and inbox item's agent name. grep -n 'approves-first?threads\\|person_name}' docs/contract.md finds them.","supersedes":"06d36deac10389c296e42470276d7a5f535689b98d1be753d0be1f645f583d9d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:30:31.539101Z","id":"a212e22cc55dcf1dbcad7306fd3b81d0fa56aa37c0136d878bb92518f3f05cec","body":{"detail":"The text line is as written, but the tool result's withheld entry is {thread_id, artifact_id, count, asked: false, no_access: true} (docs/contract.md:122-123; crates/clax-core/src/feedback.rs Placeholder; asserted in rows_on_an_artifact_the_session_may_not_read_are_held_and_told_once). An agent sent a thread on an artifact before its first take, whose access then ends, learns that artifact's ID only from this entry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3134},"end":{"line":3136},"content_hash":"4476c5f57c01898b3c87530d102614b68370d620a002bdce4e8dec9e39b7238e"},"suggested_fix":"Say 'the thread's and artifact's IDs and the count' here, or leave artifact_id out of no_access entries.","summary":"The contract says the lost-access notice carries the thread's ID and the count only; its withheld entry also carries the artifact ID","tags":["review","task:24","docs","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:58:14.169491Z","id":"ec17c3b6a225aca6867dad990faa159ca2b8d567fd706a0a79a0a2e3b2ec8fe5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:73c2b8e3","summary":"Fixed: docs/contract.md says the session is told with the thread's and the artifact's IDs and the count only (the line names the thread; the withheld entry adds artifact_id), and names a removed raise among the causes.","supersedes":"a212e22cc55dcf1dbcad7306fd3b81d0fa56aa37c0136d878bb92518f3f05cec","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:24:19.594217Z","id":"f45591f71b69438e60aebfd7b4bf854ba4d1fb1d7492685b43dd4f4339c11dd3","body":{"detail":"docs/usage.md:367 says writes need the daemon token, \"so LAN viewers can read artifacts and comment on them but not publish or change them\". With people, a connected person's agents publish, reply, resolve and write documents with key-bound grants, and their browsers approve and narrow. The guide's Use section (docs/usage.md:126-166) lists no `clax connect`, `clax people`, `clax approvals` or `clax agents rename`, says nothing of People (/people) or approvals, and nowhere says \"use a trusted LAN: Clax traffic is not encrypted\" (spec 2026-10-08 O7, §21). Only the developer note at docs/usage.md:266 and docs/contract.md describe them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":365},"end":{"line":367},"content_hash":"6a597844d96b84358c643af87ae66b0c05a053a40d9f8cf9b0b466791212e432"},"suggested_fix":"Add a short \"Working with other people\" part to Use (invite, `clax connect`, People, approvals, the not-connected switch, trusted LAN only) and rewrite the security model paragraph for grants and signatures.","summary":"The user guide's security model says LAN viewers cannot publish or change anything, and the guide never explains connecting a second person","tags":["review","final-review-ui","docs","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.305871Z","id":"52ec6e9f30f037d530b20b373fbe6a5ecee0323d788d66f764412335668f05c9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:107d63a5","summary":"docs/usage.md: a People subsection in Use (invites, requests, after connecting, agents, approvals, viewers not connected, revoking), the CLI lines for clax connect, clax people, clax agents and clax approvals, and the security model rewritten for connected people's signed requests, browser-only approvals and rights, and 'Clax traffic on the LAN is not encrypted: serve on the LAN only on a network you trust'. Checked against docs/contract.md 'People and their agents', 'Approvals', 'Names' and 'Security model'.","supersedes":"f45591f71b69438e60aebfd7b4bf854ba4d1fb1d7492685b43dd4f4339c11dd3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:21:31.835131Z","id":"4bf9be8f14c9bb823e2fc299dc181992172fb8a6e19598a4440247c1aba1caaa","body":{"detail":"The prerequisite is Node 22, the Node MODULE.bazel pins for the web, Pi and browser checks and native-check.yml installs. demo/local.ts and crates/clax-worker's scripts (e2e*.mjs, test-wasm.mjs, deploy.mjs) use no API newer than Node 22; .ts scripts run by node rely on type stripping, unflagged from Node 22.18.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":7},"end":{"line":7},"content_hash":"5e4fd852a88daddd1c554f232f5b49da8d6ad99f6f093d825f6237e288cb4ef3"},"summary":"Node 26 for development","tags":["build","revisit:a hosted or demo script needs a Node API newer than 22","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:24.147571Z","id":"cd89cedc177194b40fed826c2cfbb8aadcf00b75946a02a626b70e0da14f802f","body":{"detail":"Store::restore_version (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs) writes version.publish with an extra body field restored_from: n (the restored version) and sets carried to the paths of n, index.html aside, whose sha256 equals the previous version's, so carried keeps meaning 'unchanged from the previous version'. The row at docs/contract.md:4052 lists neither restored_from nor the restore case. The redaction table classes restored_from as safe (crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/redact.rs, body_class). Tests: store::artifacts::tests::a_restore_records_its_source_and_only_unchanged_files_as_carried and a_publish_records_no_source_version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":4052},"end":{"line":4052},"content_hash":"1b98ee2a2cf240d177ed1a6ceeb0ac292f462a2364dc06e07669afeb99d57c5f"},"suggested_fix":"Add `restored_from (n, a restore only)` to the version.publish body column and say carried lists files kept unchanged from the previous version.","summary":"version.publish gains restored_from for a restore; carried there lists only files unchanged from the previous version","tags":["docs","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:31:23.488120Z","id":"638ad98630f77762e7b7d92558445f2e8b81602f9f39af6962b14bdf30ddf7da","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7c58e3dd28c6","summary":"docs/contract.md now documents POST /api/artifacts/<id>/versions:restore under publish, and the Kinds row for version.publish names restored_from and the restore meaning of carried (git show 7c58e3dd28c6 -- docs/contract.md).","supersedes":"cd89cedc177194b40fed826c2cfbb8aadcf00b75946a02a626b70e0da14f802f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:35:44.618796Z","id":"7cb6a69070272895ae9c487f357e212cfed5a93a04d12f2eaed4fae820fcb917","body":{"detail":"docs/contract.md 'The Clax app's agent' gives the registration body as {\"harness\": \"app\", \"harness_session_id\": <install ID>, \"cwd\": \"\", \"pid\": ...}. apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart:286 builds AgentRuntime with cwd: _s.supportDir, which apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart:191 passes to HttpClaxApi.registerAppSession (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart:156-170), so the row's cwd is the app's support directory (the '' default in http_api.dart is never used by the app).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":919},"end":{"line":922},"content_hash":"9ea418c61b422418ac70ed80f532fac36901b0583ee25c6c5dcf69ec2f0e129e"},"suggested_fix":"Say \"cwd\": <the app's support directory>.","summary":"The app's session registration is documented with \"cwd\": \"\", but the app sends its application support directory","tags":["review","D1","docs","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:35:44.618888Z","id":"2ab22e89ddcbaae5d901096bcf80abe59b3e2cff06af12c94e9dcf550325929c","body":{"detail":"docs/usage.md says adb is in ~/Library/Android/sdk/platform-tools and then runs `adb devices` and `adb install -r ...` as written. `which adb` finds nothing here (only ~/Library/Android/sdk/platform-tools/adb exists), so the block fails with 'command not found' when pasted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":372},"end":{"line":379},"content_hash":"8cdb9113f3780785d6091dd24da8e6425976fce71a7051c739879800390d15dd"},"suggested_fix":"Use ~/Library/Android/sdk/platform-tools/adb in the commands, or add a line exporting PATH=\"$HOME/Library/Android/sdk/platform-tools:$PATH\" before them.","summary":"The Android steps run bare `adb`, which is not on PATH on this machine","tags":["review","D1","docs","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:35:44.619069Z","id":"3ce8945573b50018ce598527b41a86a6501c0e0e907facd18efaf5ff7782150d","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs reader_caller checks Store::may_read first (crates/clax-core/src/store/grants.rs:151: a share needs B's db.share, so a B without db is Granted only through an owner grant) and returns not_granted unless Granted; only then does it check doc_declared and return not_declared. So 'when B does not declare db it is 403 not_declared, the token included' holds only for a granted pair; an ungranted B without db answers not_granted. The page side (web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts) reports not_declared itself after reading B's declaration.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":3188},"end":{"line":3192},"content_hash":"f02b03eb15ac8c41eb21e6ece180dca001948d97da8c6a7d4bca873998054645"},"suggested_fix":"Order the sentence as the code does: without consent 403 not_granted; with consent but B not declaring db, 403 not_declared.","summary":"Over HTTP, a source without db answers not_declared only when the owner granted the read; with no grant it is not_granted","tags":["review","D1","docs","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:35:44.619204Z","id":"99932e97414db194d4c33e8a15038efc02126f22cc08a3f6b9b5fdefae4a8111","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/db.rs ids_at refuses an array longer than MAX_READ_IDS (16) before deduplicating, so 17 entries naming 2 IDs are 400 invalid_capabilities. 'at most 16 artifact IDs ... a repeated ID counts once' reads as if the limit applied after deduplication.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":3162},"end":{"line":3164},"content_hash":"4c69efa06950d51a2e63362d4b53f594e576b543eec81b12e5b562839eeb63ce"},"suggested_fix":"'Each list holds at most 16 entries ...; a repeated ID is kept once.'","summary":"The 16-ID limit counts entries before duplicates are dropped","tags":["review","D1","docs","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:36:38.269152Z","id":"4e5478faca60bc3c447e248b277fa4f21ef22c8c9aa72dab52023f7c06a3611e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7c58e3dd28c6","summary":"docs/contract.md 'The Clax app's agent' now gives cwd as the app's application support directory, as apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart:286 sends it.","supersedes":"7cb6a69070272895ae9c487f357e212cfed5a93a04d12f2eaed4fae820fcb917","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:36:38.269575Z","id":"84ddf52ae294ac68993d734abe2e049d34dbe57e046808d59d46d88b7f442823","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7c58e3dd28c6","summary":"docs/contract.md now says each list holds at most 16 entries, repeats included, and that a repeated ID is kept once after that (crates/clax-core/src/db.rs ids_at).","supersedes":"99932e97414db194d4c33e8a15038efc02126f22cc08a3f6b9b5fdefae4a8111","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:36:38.269918Z","id":"6d15370147ea3cf3383ea0bda358add4fca42bf35ea6950c4436d550c5d25379","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7c58e3dd28c6","summary":"docs/contract.md 'Reading another app's documents' now says not_granted comes first and not_declared only for a granted pair, and that the owner's page reports not_declared itself (crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs reader_caller order).","supersedes":"3ce8945573b50018ce598527b41a86a6501c0e0e907facd18efaf5ff7782150d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:36:38.270256Z","id":"33a6aa7c2e0f95690e0b3644e633f35e34b8fda1b145cb984ea0f7079d6999aa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7c58e3dd28c6","summary":"docs/usage.md's Android block now starts with export PATH=\"$HOME/Library/Android/sdk/platform-tools:$PATH\" before adb devices and adb install, so it runs as pasted.","supersedes":"2ab22e89ddcbaae5d901096bcf80abe59b3e2cff06af12c94e9dcf550325929c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:20:09.515208Z","id":"dce0e708dbd4ffbbd4bb2befc3fb8800f5c2294c1af5be02c982c554e5f3a373","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs content_policy sends only the sandbox (main origin) or frame-ancestors (artifact origin); connect-src 'none' appears only in snapshot_policy, for live pages. Either the daemon should send connect-src 'none' on app content, or this sentence (and the module comments in crates/clax-server/src/net.rs:1-3 and web/shell/src/caps/net.ts:5) should say what does keep a page from connecting.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3760},"end":{"line":3762},"content_hash":"f736141ca0b8291d6b8ac7b5c705d6810eef365e0b94e679cfa204caddd08fe5"},"summary":"The net section says an app page's content security policy keeps connect-src 'none', but artifact content carries no connect-src","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:20:09.598607Z","id":"c7ba08db1f28af9ea5ae8848a0916afb87beec9e98d85b81639b0803f6847ff7","body":{"detail":"Until the updater restores the title, icon and capabilities too, a rolled-back app keeps the update's declaration. Update this sentence if the fix changes what a rollback restores.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2106},"end":{"line":2110},"content_hash":"6c094b21858797d0bc89e4bc486a576593fe69d31ccbe976941602f238f7daa5"},"summary":"Sharing apps step 7 says the version before the update is restored, but versions:restore puts back files only (see blocker fd8f300e on apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart:446:459)","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:15.139087Z","id":"a2d8f71d280d2c5cee210c40524a4811537af80f411c7bbcf6c43fa2727d7166","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7c58e3dd28c6","summary":"Sharing apps step 7 now says the rollback publishes the version before with its files, title, icon and capabilities, the app is covered and the agent held off during the run, data/users documents are not in the snapshot, and a stale interrupted update asks Restore or Discard; docs/usage.md likewise. The behaviour landed in f1c07f346b12.","supersedes":"c7ba08db1f28af9ea5ae8848a0916afb87beec9e98d85b81639b0803f6847ff7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:49:33.998045Z","id":"97015ed52a1213c76296159d82b3bf3c0a856abc1610b706c0a9377117892ee0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Fixed in 20e1ed98c3fc: artifact content now carries connect-src 'none' and loads only its own files, assets, data: and blob: in both frame modes (crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs content_policy/load_policy); the contract's net section and security model say so (7c58e3dd28c6). Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration: 517 passed (api_content::an_artifacts_content_loads_only_its_own_files_and_connects_nowhere); npx playwright test e2e/lockdown.spec.ts: 2 passed (subdomain and sandbox: direct fetch to another host and to the daemon refused with connect-src violations, another host's <img> refused with img-src and never requested, kit modules, own image and db work); full e2e: 484 passed, 48 skipped, 0 failed.","supersedes":"dce0e708dbd4ffbbd4bb2befc3fb8800f5c2294c1af5be02c982c554e5f3a373","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:19:28.067024Z","id":"4785edb8565c8a6606d69d763cd3deee79ab81c3164051847b9fbf4efbcf9a4b","body":{"detail":"web/bridge/src/protocol.ts documents both (clax:route {depth, hash} after a welcome with app: true; clax:back {depth}). The contract's app-shell section describes clax:scroll beside them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1831},"end":{"line":1834},"content_hash":"5b27e433fc3030cf32729ff730fb1621eb76cf8887f96ac7355ff0eaf8f4be22"},"suggested_fix":"Add both next to clax:scroll in docs/contract.md.","summary":"docs/contract.md does not describe the bridge's clax:route report or the shell's clax:back order","tags":["docs","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:31:59.481288Z","id":"b3bf5e0498569277982c73432b922a69967e7d059246282de647554cbe59e291","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7c58e3dd28c6","summary":"Fixed: the Clax app section's Back paragraph describes clax:route {depth, hash} and clax:back {depth}; the claxHost table gains back(), the messages table history {back} and the Not sent notice.","supersedes":"4785edb8565c8a6606d69d763cd3deee79ab81c3164051847b9fbf4efbcf9a4b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:12:07.619009Z","id":"ecbf58834974ad92d27bd20c00f797051746b537120ba94ada74deb8c0147fd8","body":{"detail":"HomeRoute counts shownWithin from each page load it builds (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_route.dart:170-185, 198-207): the first one, and the reload after each Undo or Reset. A new version landing while the home screen shows is not timed (record 81d5a0ac9b). 'Undo last change (back to the version before the latest)' restores files only; the capabilities stay (docs/contract.md:232-248).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":559},"end":{"line":565},"content_hash":"fe20fe52c3b4f94d1b764ad529e8ccf08d637b5acb8f1755ad0367c1be435159"},"summary":"usage.md says the built-in home screen takes over when the home app has not shown within 10 seconds of a start; it is 10 s from each load of its page, and Undo keeps the declaration","tags":["review","home","docs","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:49:54.838795Z","id":"03c8f9469c17dc5dee235972b0257782003fd08daf26437922c455e72125dc57","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7c58e3dd28c6","summary":"Fixed in 7c58e3dd28c6: docs/usage.md:559-572 says the 10 s rule runs from each load of the home app's page (the first at a start, the reload after each Undo or Reset), describes the step-back Undo, and says Undo restores files only, the capabilities staying; usage.md:653-654 says the same of the Versions tab's Restore and Undo. git show 7c58e3dd28c6 -- docs/usage.md shows the change.","supersedes":"ecbf58834974ad92d27bd20c00f797051746b537120ba94ada74deb8c0147fd8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:48:34.779686Z","id":"e188686964d04e7797976a045a52971a0dd915682d9cb139f2a5370d4d3e70b2","body":{"detail":"JobsOwners::claim (crates/clax-http/src/jobs_owner.rs) spawns the drain task before answering, so when the old write ends at once the event is published before the HTTP answer is written, and the stream may deliver it first. A worker that follows the contract literally (on owner_draining, wait for held true, then claim) waits forever. The app's queue handles it (apps/clax_app/test/queue/update_test.dart, 'a drain's end heard before the claim's answer claims again'), but the contract and the route's doc comment (crates/clax-server/src/routes/jobs.rs:182-197) state only the order that follows.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2495},"end":{"line":2502},"content_hash":"cfd92fc9ebc64fbea0ed0974d898260bb9caed9b078ea9801d12acf607489e4c"},"suggested_fix":"Add to the contract: a held true heard for the client after the claim was sent counts, so on owner_draining claim again at once if one was heard.","summary":"The contract does not say that the drain's jobs_owner held true can arrive on the stream before the claim's 409 owner_draining","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.171866Z","id":"dfbad1dc2ecbe2eb3ff3aa5e6846a78a9c3fb8d7f21794972932ffbac6971be7","body":{"detail":"JobsOwners::claim (crates/clax-http/src/jobs_owner.rs) spawns the drain task before answering, so when the old write ends at once the event is published before the HTTP answer is written, and the stream may deliver it first. A worker that follows the contract literally (on owner_draining, wait for held true, then claim) waits forever. The app's queue handles it (apps/clax_app/test/queue/update_test.dart, 'a drain's end heard before the claim's answer claims again'), but the contract and the route's doc comment (crates/clax-server/src/routes/jobs.rs:182-197) state only the order that follows.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2496},"end":{"line":2503},"content_hash":"cfd92fc9ebc64fbea0ed0974d898260bb9caed9b078ea9801d12acf607489e4c"},"suggested_fix":"Add to the contract: a held true heard for the client after the claim was sent counts, so on owner_draining claim again at once if one was heard.","summary":"The contract does not say that the drain's jobs_owner held true can arrive on the stream before the claim's 409 owner_draining","supersedes":"e188686964d04e7797976a045a52971a0dd915682d9cb139f2a5370d4d3e70b2","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:48:29.105032Z","id":"b4b2294155d77685bdace9aa6060c078ee680f919c909cc4f6502a633e528c1b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7c58e3dd28c6","summary":"docs/contract.md (Jobs, the queue owner) and the claim route's doc comment (crates/clax-server/src/routes/jobs.rs) now say the drain's held true may reach the stream before the 409 owner_draining, that one heard after the claim was sent counts, and that the worker then claims again at once. Evidence: git show 7c58e3dd28c6 -- docs/contract.md.","supersedes":"e188686964d04e7797976a045a52971a0dd915682d9cb139f2a5370d4d3e70b2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:15:44.978208Z","id":"4d35601cd97c935d2127445e627941ad8ed5f40ea8a3c4afa56c4a35bd5a6867","body":{"detail":"POST /api/jobs/<id>/steps/<key> takes reply.session_id (crates/clax-server/src/routes/jobs.rs ReplyBody; Store::commit_reply_step in crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs) and uses it when the version's publishing session has ended or the version names none (a change imported from the app's ledger by crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs, or one whose session the person ended or revoked). The Dart runner in apps/clax_app still sends {threads, body, resolve, ack}; until it adds its registered session's ID as session_id on every reply step, such a change answers 400 unknown_session on each attempt.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2613},"end":{"line":2626},"content_hash":"936ba9bdb685f4171712cf5e43e45a9812653dd822cd6645d205f4396c776daa"},"suggested_fix":"In the app's job runner, set reply.session_id to the session it registered at launch (POST /api/sessions, before JobsLoaded) on every reply step.","summary":"The app's worker does not yet send session_id in its reply steps, so a change whose publishing session ended still cannot reply","tags":["app","contract","jobs","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:43:14.301581Z","id":"8788f54bab30a22089a9ffec4be9756c0e9b75e316fcf87d71d4d7cb3968b521","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"EffectRunner._reply (apps/clax_app/lib/queue/runner.dart) sends reply.session_id, the session the worker registered at launch (EffectRunner.session, WorkerAgent.session), on every reply step; without one to hand it sends the step bare and the core decides. FakeJobs (apps/clax_app/test/support/fake_core_jobs.dart) refuses unknown_session as commit_reply_step does. Evidence: bazel test //apps/clax_app:queue_runner_test //apps/clax_app:queue_reply_real_test passes at f1c07f346b12; with runner.dart from flutter-app, 4 runner tests and queue_reply_real_test (the embedded core answering the runner's Reply with Refused unknown_session on a version that names no session) fail.","supersedes":"4d35601cd97c935d2127445e627941ad8ed5f40ea8a3c4afa56c4a35bd5a6867","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:46:16.741611Z","id":"b91ee745b29b0fcd46371e1d23b740f56eb9a70c8ec8cea62c775f896c64a99e","body":{"detail":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --android now reads each launch's timings from the app's log, because a release APK is not debuggable and 'adb run-as dev.empathic.clax cat files/timings.jsonl' fails on it (the earlier script read the file that way, so it could not measure such a build either). The baseline step 5 measures the build installed on the phone, which comes from before the app ran on the embedded core and so from before the log lines: every launch would count as missing. Options: (a) take the phone baseline from a debuggable build of the baseline commit and give the script back a run-as path for it; (b) backport the clax-timing: log lines onto the baseline commit in a scratch build; (c) take no phone baseline and compare the phone against its first measured in-process build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1082},"end":{"line":1097},"content_hash":"299e52f36dd259f1a71b2741714ed1699c91f3b52ea945df12b491bd319dc4ef"},"summary":"The phone's launch baseline (step 5) cannot be taken on a release build from before 7c58e3dd28c6: it logs no clax-timing: lines and run-as cannot read its timings.jsonl","tags":["perf","android","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:07:07.074149Z","id":"5c91017d84e3ea75af5d567f8d3621c96e68fb604e89dacbff6620e1ef684a62","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:1282 sets person = false for a resolved thread, so send_target (threads.rs:1196-1235) skips the handoff_target branch and returns unknown_agent ('no live agent on this artifact has that handle', or 'not an agent handle' for a name) before send_routed can answer thread_resolved. Only a to that already owns or watches the artifact reaches send_in's thread_resolved (crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs send_in). The gallery dialog and CLI comments send --to (docs/contract.md 'comments send') would show the wrong reason. No test covers a resolved thread with a non-watching to.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1459},"end":{"line":1475},"content_hash":"64e56d14fb83e4a9415b80ede360b47e7b526392de3abb9f20e5ed3b2f5472b9"},"suggested_fix":"Check t.status == \"resolved\" in send() before send_target and return thread_resolved, or change the contract text; add a test either way.","summary":"Contract says a send naming a non-watching agent on a resolved thread is 400 thread_resolved; the daemon answers 400 unknown_agent","tags":["review","review:new-artifact","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:10:48.567809Z","id":"6b20fa29e049ec6e1477c62637de9b1b03dd14da7b617edfae3df15f7a5d5730","body":{"detail":"docs/contract.md:1470-1471 says 'a resolved thread 400 thread_resolved'. crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:1281-1283 sets person = person && t.status != \"resolved\" before send_target; with person false, send_target (:1205-1234) skips the handoff_target branch for a to that is not a live watcher and returns 400 unknown_agent ('no live agent on this artifact has that handle' or 'not an agent handle') before send_routed (:1291) is reached. grep of crates/clax-server/tests/api_briefs.rs for thread_resolved finds no case.","kind":"comment","references":"5c91017d84e3ea75af5d567f8d3621c96e68fb604e89dacbff6620e1ef684a62","summary":"confirmed: a resolved thread naming a non-watching agent answers unknown_agent, not the contract's thread_resolved","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:48:23.027070Z","id":"04b29731b85fb6cc2bf6783c54e2ca57dd3d893e4722d1e8142196bf5e62b0fa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a46ec7df2","summary":"Fixed in the code: send() answers 400 thread_resolved for a resolved thread before resolving to (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs), as the contract says. Evidence: api_briefs::the_dialog_lists_and_a_send_reaches_only_agents_that_may_read_and_watch asserts (400, thread_resolved) and no watch for a non-watching to; //crates/clax-server:integration__4 passes.","supersedes":"5c91017d84e3ea75af5d567f8d3621c96e68fb604e89dacbff6620e1ef684a62","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:23:32.344766Z","id":"d5bbb3797b32f887ce537781d285e7dd53af280aee5b5b26e390fd35d1702ccf","body":{"detail":"It says the rest of a group is \"listed by the plain query with artifact=<its ID> (or artifact=none)\". A caller that follows that literally drops the other parameters (read=unread, q, kind, agent, dates) and gets a page of the group's items under no filter, mixing read and unread. The shell repeats its filter (web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte more()), and the API test passes read=unread (crates/clax-server/tests/api_inbox.rs), but the contract does not require it.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":3136},"end":{"line":3153},"content_hash":"0adef5975912a6b033ad4d6147bf74ee71ac854bb86a38657aebd7ba2ee69ed5"},"suggested_fix":"Say: listed by the plain query with the same parameters, artifact set to its ID (or none), and before set to it.","summary":"The contract does not say a group's next_cursor pages with the same filters, read included","tags":["review","review:inbox-by-artifact","inbox","docs","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:26:04.630749Z","id":"e7e31801a972a0a6c838b4a51e054f799e285dbcdc98fac42e110d1f9fa59d75","body":{"detail":"docs/contract.md:3148-3149 reads \"`next_cursor` is the `before` of the rest, listed by the plain query with `artifact=<its ID>` (or `artifact=none`), or null.\" It does not say the group's other parameters (read, q, kind, agent, dates) must be repeated. The shell does repeat them (web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte:207, inbox.page({...filter, read: which, artifact: key}, ...)).","kind":"comment","references":"d5bbb3797b32f887ce537781d285e7dd53af280aee5b5b26e390fd35d1702ccf","summary":"confirmed: the contract names only artifact= for paging a group's rest, not the other filters","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:21:41.336972Z","id":"1979d99fb42d9498bb70b6c5859ded770e0742e29349088a04052ad4187cde25","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6fe6abb7b","summary":"Fixed: docs/contract.md says a group's rest is the plain query with the same parameters, artifact set to the group's artifact_id (or none) and before to its cursor; the route's doc comment says the same.","supersedes":"d5bbb3797b32f887ce537781d285e7dd53af280aee5b5b26e390fd35d1702ccf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:09:28.096168Z","id":"86d3418fe6db945e305c42f6a3e1629b2ee44a3b8303c46f72ba9dfbd107d2f7","body":{"detail":"The prerequisite is Node 22, the Node MODULE.bazel pins for the web, Pi and browser checks and native-check.yml installs. demo/local.ts and crates/clax-worker's scripts (e2e*.mjs, test-wasm.mjs, deploy.mjs) use no API newer than Node 22; .ts scripts run by node rely on type stripping, unflagged from Node 22.18.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":9},"end":{"line":9},"content_hash":"5e4fd852a88daddd1c554f232f5b49da8d6ad99f6f093d825f6237e288cb4ef3"},"summary":"Node 26 for development","supersedes":"4bf9be8f14c9bb823e2fc299dc181992172fb8a6e19598a4440247c1aba1caaa","tags":["build","revisit:a hosted or demo script needs a Node API newer than 22","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:45:14.254765Z","id":"ea2bf5be0ac792c6583e4e9543afc892c13d28e6de3849360aad0a5fbc7a3639","body":{"detail":"scripts/test-release-script.sh has no case for: the tag existing here or on origin on another commit (scripts/release.sh:218-221), the finished-release refusal (222-225), a checkout newer than the version or with disagreeing versions (199-202), missing tools or a non-GitHub origin; nor for resuming after the pin commit is made but not pushed, after main is pushed (steps 13-14), after a failed CI or publish-pi run, a rejected push of main, a Release run that is not listed yet when the wait starts (the fake gh lists run 101 as soon as the tag is pushed, so await_output's polling until a run appears never runs), or bazel-sync still changing files after 4 runs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":567},"end":{"line":571},"content_hash":"07e9fc5d6ae8a63e9b7ed4209240ba560c5977c7c208d8a0b90064b8f3e76e72"},"suggested_fix":"Add those cases, or narrow the sentence in docs/usage.md to what the test runs.","summary":"The release command's test is said to cover each refusal and the resumes, but several refusals and most resume points are untested","tags":["review","review:release-script","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:33.575745Z","id":"b5c0659a95c98ea6db5899e4dd04e4d6216af81789419a2d25fc29ea002ecdd2","body":{"detail":"docs/usage.md:567-571 says the test runs \"resuming after a failed just ci and after a failed or unfinished Release run, and each refusal\". scripts/test-release-script.sh's refusal cases (287-320) cover only uncommitted/untracked files, behind origin, a foreign commit, another branch, older/equal/malformed versions, a tag only origin has, gh signed out, broken signing and an unknown flag. `grep -nE 'disagree|GitHub repository|exists here|exists on origin|not on PATH|4th run'` on it finds nothing; the only \"finished\" match (228-230) is a no-op rerun, not the refusal at scripts/release.sh:222-225. GH_REPO is exported at test line 29, so resolve_repo's non-GitHub refusal (release.sh:169) cannot run. Resume cases are only at steps 4 and 8 (232-272). The fake gh (test line 84) lists run 101 as soon as the tag is on origin, so await_output's empty-poll loop is never exercised. Kind concern is right.","kind":"comment","references":"ea2bf5be0ac792c6583e4e9543afc892c13d28e6de3849360aad0a5fbc7a3639","summary":"confirmed: the test covers far fewer refusals and resume points than docs/usage.md:567-571 claims","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:46:30.660299Z","id":"3d3b93cf0bf8b28478516189285da9ae363972a266e9de6b06029dfa345f43f6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:cf9ed3d07","summary":"The listed gaps have cases in scripts/test-release-script.sh (tags on another commit here and on origin, a newer or disagreeing checkout version, a missing just, a non-GitHub origin, the pin made but not pushed, steps 13-14 after main is pushed, failed CI and publish runs, a refused push of main, a Release run listed late or never, bazel-sync that never settles), and docs/usage.md lists what the test covers, naming the refusals it leaves out (missing Bazel, python3, curl, npm, pnpm). Evidence: //scripts:release_script PASSED at 0d25dd1f7 with 52 checks.","supersedes":"ea2bf5be0ac792c6583e4e9543afc892c13d28e6de3849360aad0a5fbc7a3639","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:03:55.566260Z","id":"f0056e6622c61d913ba625b60b8fc66ca4db4898512d86c51dd7ea602dadff34","body":{"detail":"docs/usage.md:521 says the release refuses unless the checkout is 'equal to origin/main', but scripts/release.sh:321-339 accepts being ahead by the release's commits and behind once the release commit exists (the merge path). docs/usage.md:558 says the package is published 'from the pin commit, whatever main's tip is by then', but scripts/release.sh:220-227 and 652 publish from the merge commit when step 12 merged. The script header (scripts/release.sh:13-14, 'not behind origin/main') has the same gap.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":519},"end":{"line":560},"content_hash":"784fb8a28ec2c59442b5cd1b3e4a9f3185feab68d0cdd92d232265143a585278"},"suggested_fix":"Describe the actual preflight rule (behind is allowed once the release commit exists and is not on origin/main) and say 'the pin commit, or the merge on it' at docs/usage.md:558.","summary":"The Releasing section still says the checkout must equal origin/main and that the Pi package is published from the pin commit","tags":["review","review:release-script-2","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:05:39.189638Z","id":"2a04931810787dd8f033b1fb05d2703dde59a390f26bd43e37c83e52257690c1","body":{"detail":"docs/usage.md:520-522 says the release refuses unless the checkout is 'equal to origin/main'; scripts/release.sh:321-326 allows being behind once REL_COMMIT exists and is not on origin/main, and :329-339 allows being ahead by the release, pin and merge commits. docs/usage.md:557-558 says the package is published 'from the pin commit, whatever main's tip is by then'; scripts/release.sh:220-226 sets PUBLISH_COMMIT to the merge on the pin commit when there is one, and :652 dispatches with sha=$PUBLISH_COMMIT. The header at scripts/release.sh:13-14 says 'not behind origin/main'.","kind":"comment","references":"f0056e6622c61d913ba625b60b8fc66ca4db4898512d86c51dd7ea602dadff34","summary":"confirmed: the preflight and publish-commit wording disagree with scripts/release.sh","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:21:06.267634Z","id":"dd40bccc395fcb0200303866db31404ce3c50f8526193b44b859bba1e73e087c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4fde7462c","summary":"docs/usage.md and scripts/release.sh's header give the actual rule (ahead of origin/main only by the release's commits; behind only between the release commit and step 12, which merges origin/main in) and say the Pi package is published from the pin commit, or the merge on it when step 12 merged. Evidence: the text at docs/usage.md 'Releasing' and scripts/release.sh:13-20 at 4fde7462c.","supersedes":"f0056e6622c61d913ba625b60b8fc66ca4db4898512d86c51dd7ea602dadff34","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T19:04:46.728021Z","id":"f52d324a41c93afa9fbb2470bfec64a2049a088505d29026d72419e2aeedb778","body":{"detail":"Since the Clax app dropped its launch snapshot, HomeHost.call (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart, case 'shown' and case 'tiles') resolves shown() with null and takes tiles() without doing anything, and the shipped home app (apps/clax_app/home/home.js) calls neither tiles() nor reads opened. The contract text here, its copies in plugins/*/skills/clax/SKILL.md (runtime capabilities list), web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts, the app's prompt copies (apps/clax_app/assets/prompt, kept by scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh) and web/shell/src/caps/home.ts still offer both. Options: remove tiles() and the {opened} answer from the contract and every copy (an agent then stops writing tiles() calls into home apps), or keep them as documented no-ops for home apps already written.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":6036},"end":{"line":6038},"content_hash":"46b35fff334dd252970d856668c02df6b944c56dfaf93197b0af33993246a08f"},"summary":"The home capability's contract still describes the launch image: shown() resolving {opened: id} and tiles(list) kept with an image shown on the next cold start, which the Clax app no longer does","tags":["status:needs-decision","home","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:55:09.785497Z","id":"6af660c717febc8201af1b6da1eb05057743c9254c3d466289c15c3b51f1e8b4","body":{"detail":"grep -rn getApps docs plugins finds only this row. The home app (apps/clax_app/home/home.js) offers it from More and its empty state.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":6036},"end":{"line":6036},"content_hash":"33416509a2278633f3206fe649c38ba3c7c55c29c353c70e95d86ab3040dbda0"},"summary":"getApps() is in the home capability's table only: the contract's summary paragraph and the plugin skills' copies do not list it, and the Mac toolbar and app menu do not offer Get my apps","tags":["docs","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:43:06.868997Z","id":"4a14fb9d66a79949c63ec06ec5311d8bb3360aa289edfd438e33b24bc616706b","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts posts remote (the remote a linked app's thread came from, absent for one started here) on each row of the threads message, and apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart ThreadSummary.remote reads it; this table still lists {id, status, summary, label, sent, comments, version, clip}.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2604},"end":{"line":2604},"content_hash":"910d37aad696ec82bf83dc7c6868f5a6eab34f7c6d161aef8218f128e5e65623"},"summary":"The host's threads message gained remote, which the contract's Messages to the app table does not list","tags":["review","docs","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T06:07:25.957997Z","id":"6a7e10aea94fe687adfe4d6cda2c8585674a37a306e014e8c9c441f4efc451e9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fdfdf5de0","summary":"The Messages to the app table's threads row lists remote? (the remote a linked app's thread came from, absent for one started here), as web/shell/src/app/host.ts posts it.","supersedes":"4a14fb9d66a79949c63ec06ec5311d8bb3360aa289edfd438e33b24bc616706b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:59:27.479433Z","id":"8d40829145ede593ab338c16fea1db23c884fa62c4c76910c66c89cfc579d01d","body":{"detail":"POST /api/artifacts/<id>/push mode app with version and forked_from (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs push, public.rs Mode::App, push_app, app_version_key), POST /api/artifacts forked_from on a hosted Clax (routes/artifacts.rs create), and the forwarding routes of crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs exist only on akesling/app-pp-r. This text was written from `git show akesling/app-pp-r:<path>` at 9521ddfc9. On merge, check each route, body field and error code here against the merged code; the route table rows for /api/remotes/{id}/... and PUT /api/artifacts/{aid}/remotes/{rid}/bundle come with that branch's docs/contract.md change.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1290},"end":{"line":1316},"content_hash":"bfd5fc4b4492a84f2ce34f1b2142c232c54feaae1c218994e6d56095e619235a"},"summary":"The core's app mode bullet documents routes that are on akesling/app-pp-r (9521ddfc9) and not yet on this branch: re-check it once that branch merges","tags":["docs","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:59:27.479787Z","id":"18162f148aa944fdc5e2a5e537f3a4698bbbd3074b4ed81f48781634dae55203","body":{"detail":"Those are still changing on akesling/app-pp-d (373191c2b: apps/clax_app/lib/remote/sync_state.dart, merge.dart, ui/remote/diverged_sheet.dart, home_host.dart HomeApp.sync, crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_bundles.rs head's capabilities). The Tell @owner bullet here was written from that branch's ui/bundle_sheets.dart (TellOwner, tellOwnerDraft) and ui/remote/remote_flows.dart tellOwner, and the comments route it posts through is akesling/app-pp-r's POST /api/remotes/<rid>/artifacts/<raid>/comments. The Apps from the Clax app bullet 'The head' (docs/contract.md:1238-1247) lists the head's fields without capabilities, which 86357646b adds on that branch.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3329},"end":{"line":3405},"content_hash":"339aec66b125900e6718e2484fd5b616c39eeb4bd05994c27fa019bdc5cc340b"},"summary":"Linked apps does not yet describe sync states, divergence (Combine, Take theirs, Publish as a new app), forks of linked apps, the tiles' sync badges or the head's capabilities: add them once akesling/app-pp-d lands, and re-check Tell @owner","tags":["docs","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:29:52.134884Z","id":"148960ba665a836ebc5c3a1fae11f9c191b83da084b8af5d030a23a33068507e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4de5ab9e4","summary":"akesling/app-pp-r merged into this branch (5a282c5b9). The core's app mode bullet in docs/contract.md 'Apps from the Clax app' now matches the merged code: push body {mode: app, version, remote?, forked_from?, title?} and its refusals (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs push doc and checks), app_version_key's ':on:<n>' (public.rs), the forwarding routes and their sandboxed, nosniff answers (routes/remote_apps.rs), and forked_from on the hosted POST /api/artifacts (routes/artifacts.rs create). The route table rows for those routes are in docs/contract.md from the merge. ./scripts/test-plugins.sh: exit 0, 160 PASS, no FAIL.","supersedes":"8d40829145ede593ab338c16fea1db23c884fa62c4c76910c66c89cfc579d01d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:29:52.304392Z","id":"ee39be3b48863e923a107aeed6cbed03fc57adf8bdcdf384f8bc5a1f19b8b7fd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4de5ab9e4","summary":"akesling/app-pp-d merged into this branch (5a282c5b9). Linked apps in docs/contract.md now describes the sync states and tile badges as apps/clax_app/lib/remote/sync_state.dart (syncState, syncBadge) and ui/remote/remote_card.dart (syncStateLabel) give them, including the recipient's ⑂ Changed here fork state; Bring vN into mine and Diverged's three choices as remote/merge.dart (bringIntoMine, resolve) and ui/remote/diverged_sheet.dart; Publish fork with '<title> (yours)' as ui/remote/remote_flows.dart and remote/publisher.dart publishFork. The head bullet lists note and capabilities (crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_bundles.rs head). Tell @owner was checked against the merged ui/bundle_sheets.dart and remote_flows.dart tellOwner. ./scripts/test-plugins.sh: exit 0, 160 PASS, no FAIL.","supersedes":"18162f148aa944fdc5e2a5e537f3a4698bbbd3074b4ed81f48781634dae55203","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:23:01.151201Z","id":"6676fba6c14eb51db276ad6a798a7f1d3e4bc3fdf8896bc4b963e73528fd6188","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_bundles.rs:61-68 (`card`) answers name, login and public_id, used for head.published_by, head.owner, bundle.published_by and app.published_by/owner (app_bundles.rs:344, 355, 429-430). docs/contract.md:1262-1263, 1278 and the doc comments at app_bundles.rs:293 and :414 say {name, login}. Also docs/contract.md:1219 says `GET …/sharing` carries `comments`; it does only for whoever may share (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:861 vs the can_share: false answer).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1260},"end":{"line":1279},"content_hash":"b1691213da89fe65a38829ab681f2b3cdb751a4762f9f6df323df0389cda9104"},"suggested_fix":"Document public_id (null when there is none) in the contract and both doc comments, and say `GET …/sharing` carries `comments` for whoever may share.","summary":"The head's and the artifact's `app` person cards are documented as {name, login}, but the server sends {name, login, public_id}","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:23:01.151409Z","id":"e943e459fd3378d3b4e80ba66df600ad7789995f2071bcea0e18194b1517218f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:389-404 (mirrored_author_key) keys an agent comment with no person `remote:<origin>#*owner` and any other author with none `remote:<origin>#*unconnected`. docs/contract.md:1132 and :5336 name only `<public ID>`. A reader approving keys from the People page needs the two special forms.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1130},"end":{"line":1134},"content_hash":"b885fe048914275bb87643bfd0eca7d1512cabe1343a1f9540372d77d0a336c5"},"suggested_fix":"Add: an author with no public ID there is keyed `remote:<origin>#*owner` (that Clax's owner's agents) or `remote:<origin>#*unconnected` (an anonymous viewer).","summary":"The mirrored-comment visibility key is documented as remote:<origin>#<public ID>, but authors without a public ID get *owner or *unconnected","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:23:01.151595Z","id":"48f9058681c02c4a86f88fae7b73f217f278fb84b52841eecd5163100a885353","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs:297 refuse_agents gives not_for_agents for the owner's agents; another agent token is refused 403 forbidden by DeniedToGrants (crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs), and the `refusals` layer (get_page.rs:340-373) passes on only not_for_agents, turning any other 403 into the generic 404 sign-in page.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1294},"end":{"line":1296},"content_hash":"af72676b0467d2b0f09ef76dc10a785d1c82e2e2dd2b9f7a5a0e1a27caf36001"},"suggested_fix":"Say: the owner's agents are refused 403 `not_for_agents`; any other agent token gets the 404 page.","summary":"The contract says an agent is refused /a/<id>/get 403 not_for_agents; on a hosted Clax a non-owner agent token gets the 404 page","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:23:01.151773Z","id":"a40d8b0ce78b8176a89f807b1e79fb0a3f666f531d829f1a4726b1677fc194fc","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs `link` (around :285-325) forwards nothing: it writes the link locally with `url` rebuilt as `<origin>/a/<raid>` (remote_apps.rs:313), so the body's `url` field is accepted and unused. docs/contract.md:1326-1331 says 'Its other routes forward to the remote with the core's token … POST /api/remotes/<remote>/links {artifact_id, remote_artifact_id, url, remote_n}'. A caller that relies on `url` (e.g. a remote under a path prefix) gets a different link than it sent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1326},"end":{"line":1332},"content_hash":"cb58fc099458d497b98367d6b3661f26889c3644183b2f767454bd3a379801ee"},"suggested_fix":"Describe /links as a local write that needs a signed-in remote, and either drop `url` from the body (deny it) or document that the link's address is always <origin>/a/<remote ID>.","summary":"POST /api/remotes/<remote>/links is listed among routes that forward to the remote, but it only writes a local link and ignores its `url`","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:23:01.151960Z","id":"4dbd8714560194281ebd069b54a60d90a8fe498525f45e27cd525c8388a9251b","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart:166-190 shows the PublishSheet (with Include my data) only when the app has no link (`if (link == null)`); every later publish, manual or automatic, sends includeData false. docs/contract.md:3371-3373 and docs/usage.md:315-318 read as if each publish can include data. A person who wants updated seed data in v5 finds no way to send it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3370},"end":{"line":3373},"content_hash":"ac4e3b6cc127781c947a268783f22eb371e65addaac25d749a7496623fa2c576"},"suggested_fix":"Say: Include my data is chosen on the first publish (and Publish fork); later versions go up without documents. Or offer the choice on later publishes.","summary":"The contract says a publish carries documents when Include my data is on 'for that publish', but only a first publish or Publish fork offers the choice","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:23:01.152135Z","id":"6167cbeb9b1d7b17275c25d25e07d5cf0876b3f82d6008332b37fb26b66872a8","body":{"detail":"The table's texts (☁ Live, ↑ Newer here, ⑂ Changed here, ⑂ Changed in both places) are the Overview card's (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_card.dart:19-27). The app screen's pill reads '↑ v<N> here · v<M> public', '↓ v<N> ready' or 'Diverged' (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart:474-483) and shows nothing for Live, Changed here or Kept mine (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:641-657). docs/usage.md:344 ('its pill reads ⑂ Changed here') and :351 ('the app shows ⑂ Changed in both places') repeat it, and docs/usage.md:319 names a 'Publish v<N> on the app's screen' control that has no such label.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3421},"end":{"line":3434},"content_hash":"7889805a540725bdeb504e85d7acc382740ac08d31870127b69689e49b9e08c5"},"suggested_fix":"Attribute the table to the Overview card and home badge, list the screen pill's own texts, and fix docs/usage.md:319, :344 and :351 to name the controls as built (or change the pill to match).","summary":"The sync-state table is said to show as a pill on the app's screen, but the screen's pill has other texts and none for Live, Changed here or Kept mine","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:23:01.152207Z","id":"0c56b0e8e28e92fd475577b064b5f3a4bf2c4f76aac1f8defff304b5a78a5495","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs:268-285 removes the remote whatever public::revoke returns and answers `revoked: false` on failure (logged only). The app's disconnect (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart, apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart) does not read `revoked`. Offline, or against a hosted Clax without the revoke route, the token stays live on clax.dev, able to publish and change sharing as the person, while the person was told it was revoked.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":309},"end":{"line":314},"content_hash":"e0f9a09ccf5bef86a698ec9ed4f39c08b62746f9ed31eb391d6e5c81020a9474"},"suggested_fix":"Show 'Couldn't revoke this device on <host>: revoke it under People › Devices' when `revoked` is false, and word usage.md to match.","summary":"usage.md says Disconnect revokes the device, but the core forgets the remote even when the revoke fails, and the app ignores the answer","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:25:21.801623Z","id":"a6d34042ddd8620bbe6074f68f42e097ba902925bb71a22ae9223b1edf7c607b","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_bundles.rs:61-67 card() answers {name, login, public_id}, used at :344, :355, :357, :429, :430; the doc comments at :293 and :414 and docs/contract.md:1262-1263 say {name, login}. crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs:848 answers {artifact_id, can_share: false} with no `comments`; only the can_share branch (:859) adds it, while docs/contract.md:1219 says GET …/sharing carries `comments` unconditionally.","kind":"comment","references":"6676fba6c14eb51db276ad6a798a7f1d3e4bc3fdf8896bc4b963e73528fd6188","summary":"confirmed: the cards carry public_id, undocumented; GET …/sharing carries comments only when can_share","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:25:21.801872Z","id":"b10c2c1c568e90641b667f9a1381cdb783ceb7a5670951cb44d0f538ccc128d6","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:396-400 picks clax_core::visibility::OWNER for an agent with no public ID and UNCONNECTED for any other; crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:15,19 define them as \"*unconnected\" and \"*owner\", and remote_author (:30-31) formats `remote:<origin>#<id>`. docs/contract.md:1132 and :5336 name only `remote:<origin>#<public ID>`.","kind":"comment","references":"e943e459fd3378d3b4e80ba66df600ad7789995f2071bcea0e18194b1517218f","summary":"confirmed: authors with no public ID are keyed remote:<origin>#*owner or #*unconnected, which the contract does not name","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:25:21.802122Z","id":"b55420ef2516362139b9023e562008cec8213d8ff090647123b918fc76718a84","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs:1098-1102: DeniedToGrants rejects any is_grant_request (crates/clax-http/src/auth.rs:154-166, any `Bearer cxa_…`) with grants_refused, 403 `forbidden` (auth.rs:212-216); refuse_agents (agent.rs:1071-1080) gives not_for_agents only to the daemon token with a session or agent marker. crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs:341-373 passes on a 403 only when its code is not_for_agents, else returns unavailable(). docs/contract.md:1294-1295 says 'an agent is refused 403 not_for_agents'.","kind":"comment","references":"48f9058681c02c4a86f88fae7b73f217f278fb84b52841eecd5163100a885353","summary":"confirmed: only the owner's agents get 403 not_for_agents; a cxa_ agent token gets 403 forbidden, which the hosted refusals layer turns into the 404 page","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:25:21.802371Z","id":"86a3fe9c3f6eb463c1da6fe7ebdb1603009cea0c34681c1a3bcd5cf8f7c05281","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs:278-281 marks LinkBody.url #[allow(dead_code)]; link() (:292-325) rebuilds url as format!(\"{}/a/{raid}\", remote.origin) at :313 and only calls st.link_remote locally, with no request to the remote. docs/contract.md:1327-1331 lists it among 'other routes [that] forward to the remote with the core's token'.","kind":"comment","references":"a40d8b0ce78b8176a89f807b1e79fb0a3f666f531d829f1a4726b1677fc194fc","summary":"confirmed: POST /api/remotes/<remote>/links forwards nothing and ignores `url`","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:25:21.802618Z","id":"bec2688ff7d61eb942181087e4fe8eef605c3a9b73b74cb7434de8c5051ad8ad","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart:166-167 sets link null only for a fork; :183 starts includeData = false and only the `if (link == null)` branch (:186-208) shows PublishSheet and sets it from the choice. The automatic publish passes includeData: false (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart:510). docs/contract.md:3371-3372 reads 'with the documents only when Include my data is on for that publish', with no word that later publishes cannot turn it on.","kind":"comment","references":"4dbd8714560194281ebd069b54a60d90a8fe498525f45e27cd525c8388a9251b","summary":"confirmed: Include my data is offered only when the app has no link (first publish or Publish fork)","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:25:21.802884Z","id":"b9b4abab3e8662c2f0c2be59ea81583a1d668fc7e6bf7ba1dba95e16e6769e7f","body":{"detail":"syncStateLabel (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_card.dart:19-27) is the only source of '☁ Live', '⑂ Changed here' etc., used only at remote_card.dart:144 (grep of apps/clax_app/lib). The screen pill's texts are apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart:474-483 ('↑ v$version here · v$p public', '↓ v$version ready', 'Diverged'), and _pillState (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:641-657) has states only for ahead, update and diverged. No 'Publish v<N>' label exists in apps/clax_app/lib except 'Publish v$n and reply' (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart:600). docs/contract.md:3421-3423 says the table shows 'as a pill on its screen'; docs/usage.md:319, :344, :351 repeat it.","kind":"comment","references":"6167cbeb9b1d7b17275c25d25e07d5cf0876b3f82d6008332b37fb26b66872a8","summary":"confirmed: the table's texts are the Overview card's; the app screen's pill has other texts and none for Live, Changed here or Kept mine","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:25:21.803138Z","id":"c1e5388bbcf44ababd2536dcdfd0bb335c384c62befd2e6ccb2ebb840b903065","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs:271-284: a failed public::revoke only logs (tracing::warn) and sets revoked false, then remove_remote runs regardless. apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart:222-223 removeRemote discards the answer; apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart:249-257 shows a snackbar only when the call throws. docs/usage.md:313-314 says 'Disconnect revokes it'.","kind":"comment","references":"0c56b0e8e28e92fd475577b064b5f3a4bf2c4f76aac1f8defff304b5a78a5495","summary":"confirmed: the core forgets the remote whatever the revoke returns, and the app never reads `revoked`","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:53.967932Z","id":"0b0a0939ef54b9bd5cd281c27b5ee33112d73dfe4cdbc196a33f78df584c94b9","body":{"detail":"docs/contract.md now gives the head's published_by and owner as {name, login, public_id}, says published_by carries the public ID (the owner's own; null for an owner with none), and that GET .../sharing carries comments to whoever may share it. The doc comments at crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_bundles.rs:293 and :414 still say {name, login}: a crates/ edit, left for whoever owns that file. Close once they match.","kind":"comment","references":"6676fba6c14eb51db276ad6a798a7f1d3e4bc3fdf8896bc4b963e73528fd6188","summary":"Contract fixed in ce209e545; the doc comments in crates/ are left","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:53.968199Z","id":"39563f3a8864efc2a01c93a4ab5a3dbd70f2bfdd709b311f326803d691bbf3c3","body":{"detail":"docs/contract.md's home bullet in 'Runtime capabilities' now lists getApps (from a click handler, only where chrome().getApps is true). Left: apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/runtime-capabilities.md (regenerated by scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh; //apps/clax_app:prompt_sync fails until it is run), the copies in plugins/*/skills/clax/SKILL.md (~line 588, 'openSettings and importApp'), and Get my apps in the Mac toolbar and app menu (apps/).","kind":"comment","references":"6af660c717febc8201af1b6da1eb05057743c9254c3d466289c15c3b51f1e8b4","summary":"Contract summary fixed in 0e2cef5da; the skill copies and the Mac toolbar are left","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:54.556349Z","id":"a2d40c0874605018cecd21697e89b7cf16e25b7061d89545a25aff2e8db2bf00","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ce209e545","summary":"docs/contract.md (mirrored comments, and the visibility list) names remote:<origin>#*owner and #*unconnected for authors with no public ID there, as crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs mirrored_author_key keys them, and that a core signed in with an agent token keys none. Documentation only: no test applies.","supersedes":"e943e459fd3378d3b4e80ba66df600ad7789995f2071bcea0e18194b1517218f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:54.628747Z","id":"26c56fc630b25d297e0bdf1670e0ec1c67be06face5a2626bb9a3b213e3793e8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ce209e545","summary":"docs/contract.md 'Get in Clax' now says the owner's agents get 403 not_for_agents, any other agent credential 403 forbidden (crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs DeniedToGrants), and that a hosted Clax shows every refusal but not_for_agents as its 404 page (get_page.rs refusals). It also describes the 307 to a page's own get or get/index.html (get_page.rs page, Found::File). Documentation only: no test applies.","supersedes":"48f9058681c02c4a86f88fae7b73f217f278fb84b52841eecd5163100a885353","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:54.702324Z","id":"b919c24fc6b7b65fff9854f057c80d3c48188285fd9058da55ea21628fd39c93","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ce209e545","summary":"docs/contract.md describes POST /api/remotes/<remote>/links apart from the forwarding routes: a local write needing the core signed in (400 not_connected), url required and unread, the link's address always <origin>/a/<remote_artifact_id> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs link). Documentation only: no test applies.","supersedes":"a40d8b0ce78b8176a89f807b1e79fb0a3f666f531d829f1a4726b1677fc194fc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:54.774376Z","id":"3026a8a9fe1b430e0def93952e5e2f257da801dcb526a6f574a916c4c5e5074d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0e2cef5da","summary":"docs/contract.md 'Publishing' and docs/usage.md 'Publish' say Include my data is offered on a first publish and Publish fork… alone and later versions go up without documents, as apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart builds it. Documentation only: no test applies.","supersedes":"4dbd8714560194281ebd069b54a60d90a8fe498525f45e27cd525c8388a9251b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:54.850361Z","id":"a864b2639ea95229169d7127078454c266c2816a05213a672f3e74ad133767dc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0e2cef5da","summary":"docs/contract.md attributes the sync-state table to the Overview card and home badge, drops '(Publish v<N>)', lists the screen pill's own texts and taps (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart, app_screen.dart _pill), and docs/usage.md names the Overview card and the pill as built. Documentation only: no test applies.","supersedes":"6167cbeb9b1d7b17275c25d25e07d5cf0876b3f82d6008332b37fb26b66872a8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:54.926280Z","id":"2354608a3fd3534352ee3a6c7bda56871586f97277539aff6ed883612948d6cb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0e2cef5da","summary":"docs/usage.md now says Disconnect forgets clax.dev here and asks it to revoke the device, and that when clax.dev can't be reached the device stays listed under People › Devices there until revoked, as crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs remove does. The app does not yet tell the person when revoked is false (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart); that is an app change. Documentation only: no test applies.","supersedes":"0c56b0e8e28e92fd475577b064b5f3a4bf2c4f76aac1f8defff304b5a78a5495","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T15:36:04.261278Z","id":"b1bbed90901064a5dd728d2dac50de607c7a4a07f09b9d62dc96519ad6f28b59","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:554767afb52fd1524d3dbe45813efc2f733b3afd","summary":"Fixed in 554767afb: the doc comments of crates/clax-server/src/routes/app_bundles.rs head (GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/head) and stamp_app_fields now give published_by and owner as {name, login, public_id}, public_id null for an owner with none, matching docs/contract.md (fixed in ce209e545) and card(). Doc comments only; //crates/clax-server:all passes.","supersedes":"6676fba6c14eb51db276ad6a798a7f1d3e4bc3fdf8896bc4b963e73528fd6188","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T15:36:04.341588Z","id":"707126cf9425f1ceab004c806f76eb1e283e92879e1343ba328eeccb3a895595","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:032fe66341289d04ecc4eb3058f85385bf56f065","summary":"Remainder fixed: 4c09716ed lists getApps in the home capability paragraph of all four plugins/*/skills/clax/SKILL.md, word for word as docs/contract.md (scripts/sync-skill-tools.py --check exits 0; the Page contract sections equal the contract's; scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh --check prints nothing). 032fe6634 adds File > Get My Apps... (ClaxCommand.getApps, tag 31 in macos/Runner/Base.lproj/MainMenu.xib, enabled only where HomeHost.offersGetApps) and a Get My Apps item in the home toolbar on the Mac. Tests: test/ui/app_menu_test.dart 'File > Get My Apps... runs Get my apps where it is offered, and is disabled where it is not', test/home/app_screen_home_test.dart 'on the Mac, where Get my apps is offered, the home app's toolbar has Get My Apps, which runs it', test/ui/shortcuts_test.dart tag 31. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_app_menu_test //apps/clax_app:home_app_screen_home_test //apps/clax_app:ui_shortcuts_test //apps/clax_app:app_test: pass; with the menu handler or the toolbar click removed, both new tests fail. Not run on a Mac build: the xib item is checked only by tag.","supersedes":"6af660c717febc8201af1b6da1eb05057743c9254c3d466289c15c3b51f1e8b4","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.678462Z","id":"042c276e8c8d28b18c46bb7654354a6c2912b1de664beeb80a104eabb1da27e5","body":{"detail":"Since the Clax app dropped its launch snapshot, HomeHost.call (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart, case 'shown' and case 'tiles') resolves shown() with null and takes tiles() without doing anything, and the shipped home app (apps/clax_app/home/home.js) calls neither tiles() nor reads opened. The contract text here, its copies in plugins/*/skills/clax/SKILL.md (runtime capabilities list), web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts, the app's prompt copies (apps/clax_app/assets/prompt, kept by scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh) and web/shell/src/caps/home.ts still offer both. Options: remove tiles() and the {opened} answer from the contract and every copy (an agent then stops writing tiles() calls into home apps), or keep them as documented no-ops for home apps already written.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":6072},"end":{"line":6074},"content_hash":"46b35fff334dd252970d856668c02df6b944c56dfaf93197b0af33993246a08f"},"summary":"The home capability's contract still describes the launch image: shown() resolving {opened: id} and tiles(list) kept with an image shown on the next cold start, which the Clax app no longer does","supersedes":"f52d324a41c93afa9fbb2470bfec64a2049a088505d29026d72419e2aeedb778","tags":["status:needs-decision","home","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.822769Z","id":"15ca54c0075e7a1539e0ff38d9038faf6db77500be199ca7ee88a281a946e4ea","body":{"detail":"Since the Clax app dropped its launch snapshot, HomeHost.call (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart, case 'shown' and case 'tiles') resolves shown() with null and takes tiles() without doing anything, and the shipped home app (apps/clax_app/home/home.js) calls neither tiles() nor reads opened. The contract text here, its copies in plugins/*/skills/clax/SKILL.md (runtime capabilities list), web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts, the app's prompt copies (apps/clax_app/assets/prompt, kept by scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh) and web/shell/src/caps/home.ts still offer both. Options: remove tiles() and the {opened} answer from the contract and every copy (an agent then stops writing tiles() calls into home apps), or keep them as documented no-ops for home apps already written.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from docs/contract.md:6036:6038 to docs/contract.md:6103:6105: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":6103},"end":{"line":6105},"content_hash":"46b35fff334dd252970d856668c02df6b944c56dfaf93197b0af33993246a08f"},"summary":"The home capability's contract still describes the launch image: shown() resolving {opened: id} and tiles(list) kept with an image shown on the next cold start, which the Clax app no longer does","supersedes":"f52d324a41c93afa9fbb2470bfec64a2049a088505d29026d72419e2aeedb778","tags":["status:needs-decision","home","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
